# Tests follow Wine test style (snake_case; mirrors dlls/*/tests), not the NT
# kernel casing of docs/15 — so the identifier-naming check is off here. Test
# files also forward-declare Windows API names (NtCreateEvent, …) that must keep
# their PascalCase, which a naming rule would wrongly flag.
#
# Everything else comes from the root .clang-tidy: inheriting it (rather than
# re-listing the check set) is what keeps the two from drifting — the root's
# "disabled and why" list applied to the kernel only, so tests carried a few
# hundred warnings of insecureAPI/padding noise nobody could act on.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-identifier-naming
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: 'tests/'
FormatStyle: file
